<title>CANADA: Canadian foreign reserves fall in April.</title>
<headline>Canadian foreign reserves fall in April.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian foreign reserve holdings rose in April, the Finance Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>   RESERVES			  Apr 97	Mar 97</p>
<p>   Total			   19.856 bln  21.638 bln</p>
<p>   U.S. dollars		  16.980 bln  18.726 bln</p>
<p>   Other foreign currencies     503 million     499 million</p>
<p>   Gold				 148 million     150 million</p>
<p>   Special drawing rights     1.117 bln   1.134 bln</p>
<p>   IMF reserves		   1.108 bln   1.129 bln</p>
<p>Note - Figures in U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Official government operations decreased reserves by US$881 million.</p>
<p>Details of the changes in the month:</p>
<p>    Gain on gold sales		   n/a</p>
<p>    Earnings on investments	    +55</p>
<p>    Revaluation effects		  -38</p>
<p>    Foreign currency debt	     -916</p>
<p>    Other transactions		    -2</p>
<p>NOTE - in millions of U.S. dollars  </p>
<p>During April, net sales of Canada bills fell by $696.3 million, decreasing the level of outstanding bills to $5.397 billion. Sales of Canada notes decreased by $220 million, decreasing the level of outstanding notes to $1.312 billion.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
